@dmgardiner25 I think that the way you have it of `<field name>: <value` makes sense and is in line with other commands. There are too many fields in the full json API response to show, so we'll probably want to have a curated list and then just say in the help text "if you want more than these then use the API call." Vscode shows this set of properties which I think is a good starting point:

![image](https://github.com/cli/cli/assets/5447118/22062b83-e573-4f43-a1e9-27e6a60d0a14)

The other thing to consider here is a `--json` flag that can show more fields than the default `view`. For example, `gh issue view` shows title, labels, assignee, body, and a couple other things, but the `--json` option exposes even more - like `id`, `url`, `closed`, etc. So we'll probably want to form a second list of properties that aren't exposed in the default view, but are exposed via `--json` - e.g. `id`, `environment_id`, `billable_owner`, etc.
